  - education
abstract: >-
  An open book of 26 executed Jupyter notebooks, with a small Python module,
  on evaluating, propagating and reporting uncertainty: measurement and
  instruments, probability and statistics, linear, nonlinear and
  maximum-likelihood fitting, correlated data, sensitivity analysis and
  numerical error, with worked examples from physics, chemistry, chemical
  and mechanical engineering, nuclear physics, analytical chemistry and
  molecular simulation. Every chapter is mapped to the standard textbooks
  and to the GUM.
